    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40765" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rĕd-ulcĕro</span></b> , no <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>perf.</i>,
				ātum, 1, v. a., <i>to make sore again</i>, <i>to scratch
				open again.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scabram partem pumice,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					7, 5, 8</span></i>
			. — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">redulceratus dolor,</span>”
				i. e. <i>renewed</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 5, p. 163, 37</span></i>
			.</div>
